Geran-5 is a Russian jet-powered drone (6m long, 850kg takeoff weight, 90kg warhead, 1000km range, 500-600 km/h speed). 
It uses (for possibly lowest cost) a Chinese Telefly turbojet, carbon-fiber/composite airframe, commercial electronics (Chinese chips, mesh modems), 
and unified Geran parts. Low cost (around $50k after scaling) comes from simple design, COTS components, Chinese engines, 
and high parts commonality with cheaper Shahed/Geran family. Already in serial production : 500/month. Part of broader goal for tens of thousands of 
long-range drones yearly.

x15-x20 cheaper than cruise missiles like Kalibr or Flamingo. Designed for saturation attacks that need a lot of cheap mass.
